<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Selector Grammar and Escaping (EBNF)</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
selector := cursor | range | symbolic | astpath | anchor
cursor := path "@" "L" INT ":" "C" INT
range := path "@" "R(" INT "," INT "-&gt;" INT "," INT ")"
symbolic := "py://" moduleref "#" qualname ( ":" role )?
moduleref:= IDENT ( "." IDENT )*
qualname := IDENT ( "." IDENT | ":" IDENT )*
role := "def" | "sig" | "body" | "doc"
path := RELPATH | "file://" URI_PATH
anchor := "anchor://" path "#" quoted_snippet ( "?" "ctx=" INT )?
quoted_snippet := ’"’ { char | ’\"’ | ’\/’ } ’"’
</pre>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Escaping: percent‑encode <span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"># ? % " &lt;space&gt;</span> in anchor snippets and paths.
Windows paths canonicalize to <span id="A1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">file:///C:/...</span> (uppercase drive letter).</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Overloads, properties, and descriptors.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Overloaded functions can be targeted via <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">overload=<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math></span>.
Properties use role <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:sig</span> to target the getter signature; use <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:def</span> to select the backing function object.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Bundle Stability Rules</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Deterministic list ordering: <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\texttt{uri},sL,sC,eL,eC)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">uri</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\texttt{uri},sL,sC,eL,eC)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bundleId</span> := <span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sha256</span> over a JCS-canonicalized JSON of
<span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(request, resolution, facts, edits, environment, capabilities, meta*)</span>, excluding volatile fields.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Range encoding: flat <span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[sL,sC,eL,eC]</span> integer array.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Size limits: cap references to <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> entries; mark truncation and expose a pagination cursor.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Canonicalization: JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS) with UTF‑8 encoding; <span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">meta.hashing.algo = "sha256-jcs-v1"</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Dual coordinates: when CLI I/O differs from server encoding, include both coordinate systems in verbose traces; bundles retain server coordinates.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
